From: Enceka <enceka@yeah.net>
Subject: [PATCH] net: airoha: publish NPU mailbox status before the sequence trigger

Writing MBQ0_CTRL(2) advances the sequence and immediately raises the
NPU mailbox interrupt. The current sender writes the function and wait
status afterwards, allowing the NPU to dispatch the new coherent payload
using the previous slot status. This affects the shared Wi-Fi, tunnel
and PPE sender: a completion can acknowledge the previous function while
the requested function never runs.

Initialize MBQ0_CTRL(3) before advancing the sequence. Order the coherent
request payload before MMIO publication with dma_wmb(), then keep the
existing regmap writes ordered so the sequence increment is the final
request write. Preserve the per-core lock, reply copy and timeout/error
handling.

Restore the stock host order: parameter, length, status, then read and
increment the sequence. In the EN7581 firmware, the interrupt dispatcher
selects its callback from status bits 14:11 immediately after the sequence
write; it does not wait for the sender to initialize those bits later.

--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/airoha/airoha_npu.c
@@ -198,11 +198,12 @@ static int __airoha_npu_send_msg(struct
 	memcpy(core->buf, data, len);
 
+	dma_wmb();
 	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(0) + offset, core->addr);
 	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(1) + offset, len);
-	regmap_read(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(2) + offset, &val);
-	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(2) + offset, val + 1);
 	val = FIELD_PREP(MBOX_MSG_FUNC_ID, func_id) | MBOX_MSG_WAIT_RSP;
 	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(3) + offset, val);
+	regmap_read(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(2) + offset, &val);
+	regmap_write(npu->regmap, REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(2) + offset, val + 1);
 
 	ret = regmap_read_poll_timeout_atomic(npu->regmap,
 					      REG_CR_MBQ0_CTRL(3) + offset,
